-- title:
--   Witt coordinates generate a unipotent finite Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field of characteristic $p$, with $p$ prime, and let $B$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $k$-module. Assume that [`CartierDual k B`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), the $k$-linear dual $\operatorname{Hom}_k(B,k)$ equipped with its ring structure (convolution), is a local ring. For each $n$, [`Deformation.wittHom k p n B`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246) denotes the additive subgroup of the truncated Witt vectors $\mathbb{W}_n(B)$ consisting of those $x$ with $\mathbb{W}_n(\Delta)(x) = \mathbb{W}_n(\iota_1)(x) + \mathbb{W}_n(\iota_2)(x)$ in $\mathbb{W}_n(B \otimes_k B)$, where $\Delta : B \to B \otimes_k B$ is the comultiplication viewed as a ring homomorphism and $\iota_1, \iota_2$ are the two inclusions $b \mapsto b \otimes 1$ and $b \mapsto 1 \otimes b$; these are exactly the group-scheme homomorphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to W_n$. The conclusion is that the $k$-subalgebra of $B$ generated by the set of all elements $b \in B$ that occur as some coordinate $x_i$, $i \in \{0,\dots,n-1\}$, of some such $x \in$ [`Deformation.wittHom k p n B`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246), for some $n$, is the whole of $B$.
--
--   In geometric terms: for a unipotent finite commutative group scheme $H = \operatorname{Spec} B$ over a perfect field of characteristic $p$ (unipotence being expressed by locality of the Cartier dual algebra), the coordinates of the homomorphisms $H \to W_n$ generate the coordinate ring, so that finitely many of them define a closed immersion of $H$ into a finite product of Witt groups. It is one of the structural inputs to the study of the Dieudonné functor on unipotent finite group schemes, and is used in the statements about Dieudonné modules asserting injectivity of evaluation and the existence of prescribed maps under the same locality hypothesis.
-- source:
